  "worked_solution": "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}-12a+18 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-12a & =-18 \\\\ {a}^{2}-2\\cdot 6\\cdot a+{6}^{2}-{6}^{2} & =-18 \\\\ (a-6)^{2}-{6}^{2} & =-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a-6)^{2}-{6}^{2} & =-18 \\\\ (a-6)^{2}-36 & =-18 \\\\ (a-6)^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=6,q=18,$ and $p+q=24.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a-6)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\sqrt{(a-6)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\ |a-6| & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\ a-6 & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ a & =6\\pm 3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
